  "result": "I added `median` in `src/cli/median.ts` and committed it as `cc1c21b`. `npm run fast` passes.\n\n- **Behavior:** `median` throws a `RangeError` on an empty list. It sorts a copy, so the input isn't changed. For an even-length list it returns the mean of the two middle values.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/median.test.ts` covers the empty list, odd length, even length, and that the input isn't mutated. I added its weight to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Plan:** The plan is in `.krn/runs/agent/median-plan.md`, which git ignores, and I marked it done.\n- **Commit title:** The repo convention is to end the title with the task id in parentheses. My brief didn't include an id and I didn't want to make one up, so the title has none. If you give me the id, I can amend the commit.",
